 'IP addressing':[['How many bits are in an IPv4 address?',['16','32','64','128'],1,'IPv4 uses four 8-bit octets, giving 32 bits.'],['Which address is in a private IPv4 range?',['8.8.8.8','172.20.1.5','1.1.1.1','200.1.1.1'],1,'172.16.0.0 to 172.31.255.255 is private.'],['What does a subnet mask identify?',['Only DNS','Network and host portions','MAC vendor','Transport protocol'],1,'A subnet mask separates network bits from host bits.']],
 'TCP and UDP':[['Which TCP flag begins a connection?',['FIN','ACK','SYN','RST'],2,'The client starts a TCP handshake with SYN.'],['UDP is best described as…',['Connection-oriented','Connectionless','Always encrypted','A physical signal'],1,'UDP sends datagrams without establishing a connection.'],['What completes the TCP three-way handshake?',['SYN','SYN-ACK','Final ACK','FIN'],2,'The client sends the final ACK after SYN-ACK.']],
