 'Wireless and mobile':[['What does a cellular handover do?',['Changes DNS','Moves an active connection between cells','Changes IPv4 to IPv6','Creates a MAC address'],1,'Handover transfers a device connection between cell sites.'],['Wi-Fi commonly uses which IEEE family?',['802.11','802.3','802.15.1 only','802.1Q'],0,'Wi-Fi is based on IEEE 802.11.'],['What can weaken wireless signal?',['Distance and obstacles','A subnet mask','TCP ACK','DNS cache'],0,'Distance, walls and interference can reduce signal strength.']]
